.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-webhooks-reset-circuit - Close a subscription's circuit breaker and re-enable it, on any account (write mode, audited)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin webhooks reset-circuit  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Close the delivery circuit breaker of a subscription and re-enable it, whoever it
belongs to: the same write as the merchant's 'rail0 webhooks reset-circuit'.

.PP
It re-arms delivery to an endpoint the operator does not control, so check first that
the endpoint is back: 'rail0 admin deliveries --webhook  --status failed' shows
what it was failing on. Resetting a breaker in front of a receiver that still fails only
spends another 10 events reopening it. Events that fired while the circuit was open were
not delivered, and the reset does not send them.

.PP
The gateway audits it with the callback URL. No confirmation is asked: nothing is lost,
and a subscription that fails again opens its circuit again.

.PP
A write: it needs write mode ('rail0 admin write-mode on').


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for reset-circuit


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin webhooks reset-circuit 01a0f3c2-…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin-webhooks(1)\fP
